## 9. Gobuster `vhost` Mode — Virtual Host Discovery

Virtual host (vhost) mode sends HTTP requests with candidate hostnames in the `Host` header to identify websites served by the same web server.

Example:

```bash
gobuster vhost \
  -u "http://TARGET-IP" \
  --domain example.thm \
  -w /usr/share/wordlists/SecLists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt \
  --append-domain
```

#### Common Options

| Option | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `-u` | Specifies the target web server URL |
| `--domain` | Specifies the domain used for virtual-host candidates |
| `-w` | Specifies the wordlist |
| `--append-domain` | Appends the domain to candidate names |
| `--exclude-length` | Excludes responses with specified body lengths, where supported |

Confirm exact syntax with:

```bash
gobuster vhost --help
```

### Example

A wordlist entry:

```text
shop
```

With the domain appended, the candidate becomes:

```text
shop.example.thm
```

The server may return different content depending on the requested hostname, even when all requests are sent to the same IP address.

### Response-Length Filtering

Some scans produce many results because the server returns a similar default page for unknown virtual hosts.

If the installed Gobuster version supports comma-separated exact response lengths, an example is:

```bash
--exclude-length 200,300
```

This excludes response bodies of exactly 200 or 300 bytes; it does not exclude every length between those values.

Do not assume that range syntax is supported. Check the installed version's help or documentation for the accepted format.

### Interpreting Results

- `200 OK`: The server returned a successful response, which should be examined in context.
- Similar response lengths across many candidates: These may be default responses or false positives.
- No convincing result: The scan did not identify a validated virtual host with the current settings.

A negative result does not prove that no hidden virtual hosts exist. Wordlist coverage, server configuration, filtering, and the HTTP scheme can affect the outcome.

